    {
      "blockId": "tour:body:47f6c11f40afc686",
      "field": "body",
      "sourceTextSha256": "f36c8853615d4ecca87084f38b5802869bbd356b51b54632a19109c0c7f815a5",
      "text": "\nOver a week, this route connects the Andean highlands with the Caribbean coast. In Bogotá, you will see goldwork from pre-Columbian cultures and view the city from Monserrate. Next come Lake Guatavita and the underground chambers of the Salt Cathedral.\n\nIn Medellín, your introduction to Botero’s art continues with the streets of Comuna 13 and El Castillo Museum. The trip to Guatapé adds colourful façades and views of the reservoir’s islands. The final days are spent in Cartagena, walking through the old town and relaxing in the Rosario Islands.\n\n## Accommodation and prices\n\nPrices in USD by room occupancy:\n\n| Category | Bogotá, 2 nights | Medellín, 2 nights | Cartagena, 2 nights | SGL | DBL | TRP |\n|---|---|---|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| 4★ | Best Western Plus 93 Park Hotel | Poblado Plaza | Dann Cartagena | $5372 | $2829 | $2861 |\n| 5★ | Bogota Marriott Hotel | Medellin Marriott Hotel | Hyatt Regency Cartagena | $6292 | $3525 | $3150 |\n\nSGL: single occupancy; DBL: double occupancy; TRP: triple occupancy. Rates are based on services with an English-speaking guide. Other guide languages can be arranged on request. Domestic flights Bogotá → Medellín and Medellín → Cartagena, as well as international flights, are paid for separately. Exact travel dates in 2027 and the applicability of rates are confirmed at booking.\n",
